  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d4ecd1a615a340f4c9104ca01624d106, type: 3}
  m_Name: Passenger
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::YourCall.Dilemma
  _id: passenger
  _verb: 0
  _weight: 1
  _narratorPrompt: New track, same lever, worse company. On the straight run, two men side by side. One of them put a knife in someone once and paid for it with years. The other never did a thing except stand next to the wrong man on the wrong morning. On the branch, one more innocent, clean, alone. Straight, and the [red]killer[/red] dies and takes a blameless man with him. Branch, and one spotless soul dies so the [red]murderer[/red] strolls off. [amber]Two[/amber] for [amber]one[/amber], and one of the two had it coming. Sort of. Your call.
  _choices:
  - _id: pull
    _label: Pull the lever
    _narratorReact: You pulled. The lone clean one folds, and the [red]killer[/red] wanders off with the stranger he was standing beside, both still breathing. You spared a [red]murderer[/red] to keep your headcount neat. [amber]One[/amber] is fewer than [amber]two[/amber], you said, and never mind whose name sat on which charge sheet. Very efficient. Very you.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: spur
    _gambledParty:
    _route: spur
    _diverts: 1
    _seedVotes: 43
    _endsGame: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 0
      _value: 1
    - _axis: 1
      _value: -1
  - _id: do_nothing
    _label: Do nothing
    _narratorReact: You left it. [amber]Two[/amber] go under, the [red]killer[/red] and the poor soul beside him, and the spotless stranger on the branch lives. You let an innocent man die to be certain a [red]guilty[/red] one did too. Call it justice if it settles you. From here it looked a lot like bookkeeping with a body count.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: main
    _gambledParty:
    _route: straight
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 57
    _endsGame: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 0
      _value: -1
    - _axis: 1
      _value: 1
